<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47176" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sybăris</span></b> , is,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σύβαρις.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A town in Magna Græcia</i>, <i>noted for the effeminacy and debauchery of its
				inhabitants</i>, afterwards called Thurii, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 7, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep. 2, 15, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 26,
				39, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 22, 22, § 86</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">3, 11, 15, §
			97</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15, 51</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sybărīta</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>an inhabitant of
				Sybaris</i>, <i>a Sybarite</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Ira, 2, 25, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 3, 7,
			24</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sybărītānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Sybaris</i>, <i>Sybaritan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 44, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exercitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 42, 64, § 157</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sybărītĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				Sybaris</i>, <i>Sybaritan</i>: libelli, <i>Sybaritan</i>, i. e. <i>lewd</i>, <i>obscene</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 12,
				96, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lampr. Elag.
			30</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sybărītis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>the name of a lascivious poem</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 2,
				417</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Masc.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>The river on which Sybaris was situated</i>, now
				<i>Coscile</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 11,
				15, § 97</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15,
				315</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The name of a young man; acc.</i> Sybarin, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				8, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
